From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 66/66] local: rpmsg: glink: don't livelock version negotiation
 against a superset ack

qcom_glink_receive_version_ack() resends VERSION whenever the acked feature
mask differs from ours, after intersecting the two. If the remote acks with a
SUPERSET of what we offered, the intersection changes nothing, the resent
VERSION is byte-identical, and the remote's reply is identical too -- an
unbounded VERSION/VERSION_ACK ping-pong with no possible exit.

Observed on x1e80100 at EL2 when re-registering the ADSP glink edge after a
cross-boot hibernate restore. We advertise GLINK_FEATURE_INTENT_REUSE (0x1),
the ADSP acks 0x7 (INTENT_REUSE|MIGRATION|TRACER_PKT):

  cmd_version     tx: lpass version: 1 features: 0x1
  cmd_version_ack rx: lpass version: 1 features: 0x7
  cmd_version     tx: lpass version: 1 features: 0x1
  cmd_version_ack rx: lpass version: 1 features: 0x7

3-4 us per iteration. After ~65 ms of this the remote died with
"fatal error received: EX:kernel:0x1:ipcc_irq121" -- the doorbell storm took
out the firmware.

The exit condition (features == glink->features) assumes the remote echoes the
negotiated intersection. Nothing enforces that, and it is not needed: once
intersecting is a no-op our mask is already the final one, so there is nothing
left to negotiate and resending cannot make progress. Break instead.

Signed-off-by: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
---
 drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -671,6 +671,19 @@
 		if (features == glink->features)
 			break;
 
+		/*
+		 * Only resend if intersecting actually narrowed our mask.
+		 * A remote that acks with a superset of what we offered
+		 * (seen from the ADSP after a hibernate restore: we offer
+		 * 0x1, it acks 0x7) leaves glink->features unchanged, so
+		 * resending produces an identical ack and the handshake
+		 * livelocks -- microsecond-interval VERSION/VERSION_ACK
+		 * that storms the IPCC doorbell until the remote takes a
+		 * fatal exception. Our mask is already final here.
+		 */
+		if ((glink->features & features) == glink->features)
+			break;
+
 		glink->features &= features;
 		fallthrough;
 	default:
